# Engineering Focus

NeuraBot brings together multiple engineering disciplines into one integrated platform:

```text
        MECHANICAL DESIGN
               │
               ▼
       ELECTRICAL SYSTEMS
               │
               ▼
      EMBEDDED CONTROL
               │
               ▼
     ROBOTICS / KINEMATICS
               │
               ▼
       AI PERCEPTION
               │
               ▼
    HUMAN–ROBOT INTERACTION
               │
               ▼
        SYSTEM INTEGRATION
```

The project demonstrates the development of a robotic system from **physical design and fabrication through embedded control, robotics algorithms, AI integration and operator interaction**.

---

# Project Philosophy

NeuraBot is built around a simple engineering principle:

> **Integrate the physical, computational and intelligent layers of a robot into one coherent system.**

The project therefore treats the robot not as a collection of independent components, but as a complete engineering system in which:

**Mechanical Design**

→ provides the physical platform

**Embedded Control**

→ drives the actuators

**Robotics Algorithms**

→ generate movement

**AI**

→ provides perception and interaction

**Power Management**

→ monitors the electrical system

**Web Interface**

→ connects the operator to the robot

---

# Status

🟠 **In Development**

NeuraBot remains an evolving robotics platform.

The current repository documents the project's **mechanical design, hardware architecture, system integration, control capabilities, AI subsystems and development roadmap**.

Future development will expand the platform toward greater autonomy, environmental mapping, expressive interaction and robotics middleware integration.

